# Adaptive EO Field-of-View Management Algorithm

This project implements an adaptive Field-of-View (FOV) management algorithm for an electro-optical camera using MATLAB/Simulink.

The algorithm automatically switches between Wide FOV and Narrow FOV modes according to target range, tracking confidence, target pixel size, and target position inside the camera field of view.

## FOV Modes

### Wide FOV

- Horizontal FOV: 30°
- Provides wider scene coverage
- Used for target acquisition and maintaining situational awareness

### Narrow FOV

- Horizontal FOV: 8°
- Provides higher pixel density on the target
- Used when target conditions are suitable for detailed observation

## Wide → Narrow Transition

The algorithm switches to Narrow FOV when:

- Track confidence ≥ 0.72
- Target size ≥ 3 pixels in Wide FOV
- Target is inside the Narrow FOV
- Conditions remain valid for 2 seconds

## Narrow → Wide Transition

The algorithm returns to Wide FOV when one of the following occurs:

- Track confidence ≤ 0.50
- Target pixel size becomes too small
- Target leaves the Narrow FOV

A confirmation delay is applied to prevent unnecessary mode switching.

## Scenario Generator

Different `scenarioID` values are used to generate irregular and repeatable target scenarios.

The following parameters vary during simulation:

- Target range
- Track confidence
- Target azimuth

## Outputs

- Active FOV Mode
- Active Horizontal FOV
- Pixels on Target
- Wide FOV Pixel Count
- Narrow FOV Pixel Count
- Target In/Out of FOV

This model demonstrates adaptive optical mode management for EO tracking applications.
